# tasks_objlist_record_at_end: A buffer record that ends exactly at the task's end: in-process record reads copy out of the task, which refuses `end >= taskLength`, so the buffer cannot be created and the exec faults; the service reads in place and accepts `end == taskLength`, and the fill lands (section 7.1). A record one byte shorter works everywhere.
